      "message": "Be careful with not adopting the shell permission without specifying which permissions to adopt.\n\nIIRC the behaviour of the adoptShellPermissionIdentity overload that specifies permissions and the overload that does not specify permissions is very different - the one that does not specify permissions changes your UID as well, which tends to break things pretty badly if any other thread is running in the background.\n\nBasically, I think we should basically always use runAsShell and always specify permissions. But for this CL you can just add NETWORK_SETTINGS explicitly, and add a TODO to use runAsShell, and file a bug to move this test to runAsShell?",
