      "side": 1,
      "message": "This removes *all* UIDs from the chain, not just the one that is being tested, right? And we can\u0027t restore the chain to its previous contents?\n\nIf so: this might be OK for OEM chain 2, since it\u0027s unused in AOSP. Not sure if it\u0027s OK for the background chain though. This code might make subsequent tests flaky. We may need a hidden method in CM that we can call to find all the UIDs in the chain so we can then restore them.\n\nIf you want to merge this CL as is, that might be OK but please add a comment that explains that this completely clears the chain. Something like:\n\n    // Note that this removes *all* UIDs from the chain, not just the UID that is\n    // being tested. This is probably OK since FIREWALL_CHAIN_OEM_DENY_2 is unused\n    // in AOSP and FIREWALL_CHAIN_BACKGROUND is probably empty when running this\n    // test (since nothing is in the foreground).\n    //\n    // TODO: add a getFirewallUidChainContents or similar method to fetch chain\n    // contents, and update this test to use it.",
